    {
      "id": "claim_11517f4004d84d74a9aa5799a8d72849",
      "statement": "All curated tool modules live flat under openswe/tools/ and are re-exported through openswe/tools/__init__.py with a _TOOL_MODULES map, which lazily imports and caches each export; several names can share an implementation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/tools/__init__.py#L5-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e7ee23679dbaaa271294593f1e38c02fe78b137c6ce1743fe13e8873ccb4424:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b823ac1ae2804800ae8f17a8a5d42f91",
      "statement": "openswe/server.py:get_agent assembles the main coding agent's static_tools list covering web access (http_request, fetch_url, web_search), plan lifecycle (save_plan), background execution (background_execute, background_task), user instructions and skills (save_user_instructions, save_user_skill, delete_user_skill), thread operations (list_threads, get_thread, manage_thread, start_thread), PR creation (open_pull_request, link_pull_request, search_pull_requests), PR review operations (expedite_pr_approval, merge_expedited_pr, request_pr_review), human reviewer operations (request_human_review, assign_human_reviewer, auto_assign_human_reviewer, dismiss_human_review_request, get_human_review_status), feedback (submit_thread_feedback, submit_review_assessment_feedback), baby-sit management (manage_baby_sit), sandbox recovery (recreate_sandbox), scheduling (schedule_thread_wakeup, request_rollout_check), user-settings lookup (read_user_settings) and optional mutation (save_user_settings), platform-issue reporting (report_platform_issue), Slack tools, incident management (manage_incident), code-channel management (manage_code_channel, code_channel_set_view), event operations (listen_events, list_event_types), optional Notion task comments (comment_on_notion_task) and design tools, SQL queries (read_only_sql), store operations (read_store_item), sandbox download tools (output_iframe, create_sandbox_file_download_url, expose_port when enabled), design and review tools (propose_review_comment, propose_pr_review), optional CLI result logging, optional desktop worktree handoff, feature flags and review policy (manage_feature_flags, manage_review_approval_mode, manage_review_repos), and admin tools (conditionally).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/server.py#L1801-L1882",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6196eb56177d0f9af4bf590b4cc7b646d0004042fc2105cf17d0b39d6ed9ce1b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ec4ebfd8391b4df9a982288c88182ba1",
      "statement": "The main agent's tool list is dynamic: admin threads add ADMIN_TOOLS (automation operations create/update/delete/trigger/list, workspace management list/publish/refresh/configure/delete, organization-skill operations save/delete), desktop local_run collapses to just http_request/fetch_url/web_search, stop_summary_mode collapses to slack_read_thread_messages/slack_reply, Slack tools are removed when Slack is not enabled with scheduled runs keeping slack_list_channels/slack_post_message, Slack DM concierge mode removes slack_add_reaction, personal user-settings tools are removed when no credential login is verified, human review tools are removed when Slack bot context unavailable, expedited review tools are removed when disabled or Slack bot context unavailable, incident tools are conditionally added with automatic sweeps excluding mutations, and the subagent excludes save_user_settings and sandbox_only_tools.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/server.py#L1783-L1832",
